}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Green Egg: N208''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Combat Crawfish Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]].

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
These forms are <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]], this unit is not meant to be used before its True Form. However, due to its somewhat low cost and quick recharge, reverting to this form may prove useful if a cheaper, more spammable meatshield is needed in an [[Underground Labyrinth]] or [[Legend Quest]] stage.

==='''True Form'''===
Combat Crawfish Cat is a subpar meatshield who is not worth considering in any serious capacity. Against Angels, Combat Crawfish Cat is entirely outclassed by [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]], who boasts almost double its base HP, while being cheaper and having a faster recharge. This crawfish's comparatively high speed is not nearly enough to justify using it in most circumstances, and the gap in performance only widens as the player obtains more +levels and [[Talents]] on their Ramen Cat. Even vs. [[Angelic Beast Rajakong]], it lacks the bulk to withstand Rajakong's offensive onslaught for very long, especially given how it has two knockbacks.

Against Floating, things become a little more favorable for Combat Crawfish Cat. There is a distinct lack of anti-Floating meatshields for a majority of The Battle Cats's progression, but fitting this unique niche doesn't save it from mediocrity. A large majority of the Floating trait is infested with high-pressure enemies who deal ungodly amounts of damage. Unless boosted to Lv.50+10, there's no hope of it withstanding even brief confrontations with pushers like [[Teacher Bun Bun]] variants, [[Brollow]]s, [[Raging Bahamut Cat]], and the likes. Therefore, the best-case scenario for Combat Crawfish Cat is to fend off enemies with high damage, but slow attack rates, such as [[Owlbrow]], [[Cli-One]], and [[Crazed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Flying Cat]]. Notably, [[Behemoth Slayer]] gives it an especially good matchup into [[Pterowl Hazuku]]. It's fast enough to slip into his blind spot if need be, and can withstand a few hits from him otherwise, in spite of its lack of Surge Immunity. In most other matchups, Behemoth Slayer is mostly cosmetic, as you'd effectively be throwing the poor thing into a boiling pot. Keep in mind that Combat Crawfish Cat is eventually outclassed by [[Carpenter Cat (Rare Cat)|Rapper Cat]] late in the game.

While it can ''technically'' survive an attack from [[Ensanglion the Calamity]], this is incredibly impractical. It requires Combat Crawfish to be at Lv.50+10 and have a +30% HP boost from Defense and/or Resist Cat Combos, which can take anywhere from 3 to 5 additional slots. Superior choices like [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Cat]], [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]], or [[Killer Cat (Rare Cat)|Radical Cat]] need neither Cat Combos nor Lv.50 to do this.

